 "format": "rustsheet-case/v1",
 "description": "FIN-02 (val5): Excel's Stirling error at a count that is not whole, read through the beta density at x = k/n, where both deviances bd0(k, n x) and bd0(n-k, n(1-x)) are exactly 0 (n a power of two, so k/n, n x and n(1-x) are exact; column G checks n x). There lc = S(n) - S(k) - S(n-k) with nothing else in it, so each cell pins S(k) + S(n-k) to about 1E-17 given S at the whole n. 53 cells: every half-integer k below n for n = 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 and quarter and eighth counts at the small n. A fresh test of the rule T-5107 identified on other cells (statistics.md \"Stirling error at a count that is not whole: a walk up to the series\"); decision 0188 R4.2. Frozen engine values: docs/research/val5-fin-predictions.json (hypotheses, NOT expected values). Precision!B2:B4 must retain 0.9999999999999998, 1, 1.0000000000000002; C2:C4 must be -1,0,1.",
